---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import {
  PlanOutlineLongContent,
  PlanOutlineMarks,
  PlanOutlineNested,
  PlanOutlineNotices,
  PlanOutlinePlayground,
  PlanOutlineStates,
  PlanOutlineViewer,
} from '../../components/PlanOutlineDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Plan Outline"
  description="A saved agent plan as a read-only outline of nested tasks, with marks, progress, and dependencies."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Plan Outline</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A saved agent plan as a read-only outline. The header shows the plan's status, a progress bar, and notices. Groups
    list their tasks. Each task opens to show its brief, what “done” means, what it waits for, and actions.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <PlanOutlinePlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A running plan with one group"
      code={`import { PlanOutline, type PlanOutlineTask } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/plan-outline";
import { Database } from "reicon-react/icons/Database";

const tasks: PlanOutlineTask[] = [
  {
    id: "research", title: "Research", mark: "running", label: "1 of 2 done",
    children: [
      { id: "audit", title: "Audit last spring's catalog", mark: "done", label: "Done", assignee: "Main agent",
        typeIcon: { icon: <Database />, label: "Table" } },
      {
        id: "suppliers", title: "Confirm supplier stock", mark: "running", label: "Working",
        criteria: ["Each variety has a confirmed count."],
        dependencies: [{ id: "audit", title: "Audit last spring's catalog", label: "Done" }],
      },
    ],
  },
];

<PlanOutline
  title="Launch the spring bulb catalog"
  status="Running"
  tone="active"
  progress="1 of 2 done · 1 working"
  tasks={tasks}
/>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>title</code>, <code>brief</code>: the plan name (an <code>h3</code> that also names the section) and one
        paragraph under it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>status</code> and <code>tone</code>: the badge text and its color. <code>tone</code> is{' '}
        <code>active</code>, <code>attention</code>, <code>done</code>, <code>failed</code>, or <code>neutral</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>progress</code>: the line under the bar, in words. The bar has one segment per task; cancelled tasks are
        left out.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>notice</code> and <code>stale</code>: any content under the progress, such as an{' '}
        <a href="/components/alert/">Alert</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>tasks</code>:{' '}
        <code>
          {
            '{ id, title, mark, label, typeIcon?, assignee?, brief?, criteria?, dependencies?, reason?, action?, children? }[]'
          }
        </code>
        . A task with <code>children</code> is a group.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Optional <code>typeIcon: {'{ icon, label }'}</code> identifies the resource type beside its independent status
      mark. Supply a decorative icon and a plain type name such as “Table”. The type name is available to screen readers
      and as a native tooltip. It is not the task's assignee. Without this field, row layout is unchanged.
    </p>
    <p>
      Plan Outline has one look and one size. Map your own plan data to tasks in an adapter, as the examples here do. It
      never ticks, edits, reorders, or assigns tasks.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Marks and tones</h2>
    <p>
      Seven marks: <code>pending</code> (clock), <code>running</code> (spinner),
      <code>attention</code> (question), <code>blocked</code> (lock),
      <code>done</code> (check), <code>failed</code> (warning), and
      <code>cancelled</code> (crossed out). Every mark has a text
      <code>label</code>, so color is never the only signal.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <PlanOutlineMarks client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Nested groups</h2>
    <p>
      Groups start open and can nest. A group's <code>brief</code> shows above its tasks. A group with no tasks says so.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <PlanOutlineNested client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="details">
    <h2 class="section-title">Task details</h2>
    <p>
      A task with a <code>reason</code>, <code>brief</code>,<code>criteria</code>, <code>dependencies</code>, or{' '}
      <code>action</code>
      opens to show them. A failed task's reason is red. Each dependency links to its row and moves focus there, opening
      its group if it was closed. Tasks with none of these are plain rows.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      code={`{
  id: "pricing",
  title: "Set prices for the spring catalog",
  mark: "attention",
  label: "Needs your review",
  assignee: "Pricing analyst · created for this plan",
  brief: "Use last year's margins and current supplier quotes.",
  criteria: ["No variety sells below a 35% margin."],
  dependencies: [{ id: "audit", title: "Audit last spring's catalog", label: "Done" }],
  action: (
    <Button variant="outline" size="sm" nativeButton={false} render={<Link to={taskUrl} />}>
      Review in task
    </Button>
  ),
}`}
    />
    <p>
      Pick “Waiting on you” or “Verified” in the playground above to open a task with an action or a verification
      report.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Notice and stale data</h2>
    <p>
      Put alerts and requirement checks in <code>notice</code>. When a refresh fails, keep the last plan and say so in{' '}
      <code>stale</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <PlanOutlineNotices client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Someone else's plan</h2>
    <p>
      People who did not start the plan see who a task waits for, such as “Waiting for a review”. The link to the task
      stays, so they can open it.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <PlanOutlineViewer client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Loading, error, and empty</h2>
    <p>
      Before a plan loads, show <a href="/components/skeleton/">Skeleton</a>
      lines. When it can't load, use a <a href="/components/state-panel/">State Panel</a>. A plan with no tasks says
      none were added yet.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <PlanOutlineStates client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Long content</h2>
    <p>Long titles, names, and links wrap. Labels stay at the end of the row.</p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <PlanOutlineLongContent client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The outline is a <code>section</code> named by its title. Tasks are ordered lists named “Tasks” and “Group tasks”.
      Rows with details are buttons with <code>aria-expanded</code>; Enter and Space open them. Mark icons and the bar
      are hidden from screen readers; the label and progress text say the same.
    </p>
    <p>Rows open in 180ms and chevrons turn in 120ms. With reduced motion they change at once and the spinner stops.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Running uses <code>--sprout-info</code>, attention
      <code>--sprout-warning</code>, done <code>--sprout-success</code>, failed
      <code>--sprout-danger</code>, and pending, blocked, and cancelled
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>. Rows hover with <code>--sprout-hover</code>, lines use <code>--sprout-line</code>,
      and links
      <code>--sprout-primary</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
